/* VT_BLOBOBJECT
 * linkage: own-page (2 statement(s), e.g. corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/aa519284(v=msdn.10).html)
 * row (table): VT_BLOBOBJECT 70 blob A blob member containing a serialized object in the same representation that would appear in VT_STREAMED_OBJECT. That is, a DWORD byte count (where the byte count does not include the size of itself) which is in the format of a class identifier followed by initialization data for that class. The only significant difference between VT_BLOB_OBJECT and VT_STREAMED_OBJECT is that the former does not have the system-level storage overhead that the latter would have, and is therefore more suitable for scenarios involving numbers of small objects.
 * source: corpus/learn/windows-ce-5.0/aa519284(v=msdn.10).html
 * row (table): VT_BLOBOBJECT 70 blob A blob member containing a serialized object in the same representation that would appear in VT_STREAMED_OBJECT. That is, a DWORD byte count (where the byte count does not include the size of itself) which is in the format of a class identifier followed by initialization data for that class.
